{"name":"Bull Ring","hex":"#6b605b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bull ring","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The area in which bullfighting takes place.","An unusually short track, typically six furlongs or less for one lap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bull_ring"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bullring","blocks":[{"text":"A bullring is an arena where bullfighting is performed. Bullrings are often associated with the Iberian Peninsula, but they can also be found through Iberian America and in a few Spanish and Portuguese ex-colonies in Africa. Bullrings are often historic and culturally significant centres that bear many structural similarities to the Roman amphitheatre."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Spain_Andalusia_Malaga_BW_2015-10-24_09-52-48.jpg/330px-Spain_Andalusia_Malaga_BW_2015-10-24_09-52-48.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bullring"},{"title":"Bull Ring, Birmingham","blocks":[{"text":"The Bull Ring is a major shopping area in central Birmingham, England, consisting of open-air and indoor market stalls as well as a large indoor shopping centre."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Aerial_Bull_Ring_Birmingham.jpg/330px-Aerial_Bull_Ring_Birmingham.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bull_Ring%2C_Birmingham"},{"title":"Bull","blocks":[{"text":"A bull is an intact adult male of the species Bos taurus (cattle). More muscular and aggressive than the females of the same species, bulls have long been an important symbol in many religions, including for sacrifices. These animals play a significant role in beef ranching, dairy farming, and a variety of sporting and cultural activities, including bullfighting and bull riding."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/A_F